576
01:18:13,006 --> 01:18:22,084
所以每个工具都在简单的接口背后封装了复杂的 Business 逻辑，
智能体可以轻松理解并利用这些工具。
So each tool encapsulates complex business logic behind a simple interface that the agent can easily understand as well as utilize.

577
01:18:23,598 --> 01:18:32,356
现在，最终的输出展示了智能体将多个工具的信息综合成连贯且有用的回答的能力。
Now the final output demonstrates the agent's ability to synthesize
information from multiple tools into a coherent and helpful response.

578
01:18:33,294 --> 01:18:38,532
在这种情况下，回答是：您的订单 ORD123 已经发货。
In this case, the response is your order, ORD123, has already shipped.

579
01:18:39,086 --> 01:18:42,436
您可以使用物流单号 TRK456 进行查询。
You can track it using the tracking number TRK456.

580
01:18:43,278 --> 01:18:47,844
如果您还有任何问题或需要帮助，请随时提问。
If you have any further questions or need assistance, feel free to ask.

581
01:18:48,462 --> 01:19:00,996
所以这个响应表明，智能体不仅执行了必要的工具，还根据它最终收集到的信息，
应用了Business逻辑来确定合适的行动路径。
So this response shows that the agent not only executed the necessary tools, but it also applied business logic to determine the
appropriate course of action based on the information that it ended up gathering.

582
01:19:02,158 --> 01:19:10,948
这种编排方法让AI智能体能够处理复杂的、需要推理和行动的多步骤流程。
So this orchestration approach enables AI agents to handle complex and
multi-step processes that require both reasoning as well as action.

583
01:19:11,824 --> 01:19:24,644
智能体充当智能协调者，它理解Business流程，选择合适的工具，逻辑性地排列这些工具，
然后将结果综合成有意义的产出。
The agent serves as an intelligent coordinator that understands business processes, selects appropriate tools,
sequences those tools logically, and then it synthesizes the results into meaningful outcomes.

584
01:19:26,094 --> 01:19:36,784
现在，这把静态的AI模型转变为动态系统，能够以高
度专业且可靠的方式处理现实世界的Business场景。
Now this transforms static AI models into dynamic systems that are capable of
handling real-world business scenarios with sophistication as well as reliability.

585
01:19:36,974 --> 01:19:42,660
现在，我们需要解决在构建复杂的AI智能体系统时出现的一个关键挑战。
Now we need to address a critical challenge that emerges when building sophisticated AI agent systems.

586
01:19:43,534 --> 01:19:46,820
那就是智能体工具的互操作性问题。
The problem of interoperable agent tooling.

587
01:19:47,854 --> 01:20:00,196
当我们检查规划-行动接口时，这个挑战就变得显而易见了，
它是智能体的思考过程与其执行现实任务能力之间的关键连接点。
Now, this challenge becomes apparent when we examine the plan action interface, which is the crucial connection point between an
agent's thinking process and its ability to execute real-world tasks.

588
01:20:01,518 --> 01:20:10,820
现在，让我解释一下我们所说的规划-行动接口是什么，以及为什么它是一个如此重大的挑战。
Now, let me explain what we mean by the plan action interface and also why this presents as such a significant challenge.

589
01:20:12,110 --> 01:20:29,188
规划-行动接口代表了智能体规划模块（决定要做什么）与其行
动模块（使用可用工具集实际执行这些决策）之间的通信路径。
The plan action interface represents the communication pathway between an agent's planning module where it decides what needs to be
done, and its action module, where it actually executes those decisions using the set of available tools.

590
01:20:30,286 --> 01:20:39,972
你可以把它想象成大脑决定写信，以及手握笔并形成文字之间的连接。
Now you can kind of think of this like the connection between your brain deciding
to write a letter and your hand actually holding the pen and forming the words.

591
01:20:41,326 --> 01:20:49,764
意图与执行之间的接口必须是无缝且可靠的，系统才能高效运行。
The interface between the intention and execution must be seamless as well as reliable for the system to work efficiently.

592
01:20:51,342 --> 01:21:01,188
现在，当我们观察不同的AI框架如何实现这个接口时，智能体工具互操作性的挑战就变得清晰了。
Now, the challenge of interoperable agent tooling becomes clear when we examine how different AI frameworks implement this interface.

593
01:21:02,094 --> 01:21:07,620
现在考虑两个流行的智能体框架：LangGraph和CrewAI。
Now consider two popular agent frameworks Langgraph and Crew AI.

594
01:21:09,102 --> 01:21:20,490
这两个框架都是为了创建能够规划和执行行动的智能体而设计的，
而且它们可能都需要访问相同的底层系统，比如用于信息检索的Google Search，
Both of these frameworks are designed to create intelligent agents that can plan and also execute actions,
and both might need to access the same underlying system, such as Google

595
01:21:20,490 --> 01:21:21,880
这两个框架都是为了创建能够规划和执行行动的智能体而设计的，
而且它们可能都需要访问相同的底层系统，比如用于信息检索的Google Search，
Search for Information Retrieval or a Postgres database for data storage.

596
01:21:21,880 --> 01:21:25,284
或者用于数据存储的Postgres数据库。
Search for Information Retrieval or a Postgres database for data storage.

597
01:21:26,286 --> 01:21:39,588
然而，每个框架处理规划-行动接口的方式都是特定于实现
的，这意味着它们使用不同的方法、协议以及数据格式。
However, the way that each framework handles the plan action interface is implementation specific,
meaning that they use different approaches, protocols, as well as data formats.

598
01:21:41,038 --> 01:21:48,100
现在，这造成了一个重大问题，正如两个实现之间的红色X所示。
Now, this creates a significant problem that is illustrated by the red X between the two implementations.

599
01:21:49,422 --> 01:22:06,404
尽管LangGraph实现和CrewAI实现都需要执行相似的任务并访问相同的底层系统，
但问题在于它们无法轻松共享工具或相互通信。
Even though both the Line Graph implementation and the Crew AI implementation need to perform similar tasks and also access the same
underlying systems, the problem here is that they cannot easily share tools or communicate with each other.

600
01:22:07,438 --> 01:22:15,268
这就像是两个精通各自领域但语言不通的专家，试图共同合作完成一个项目。
So it's kind of like having two brilliant specialists who speak different languages trying to collaborate on a project together.

601
01:22:16,174 --> 01:22:29,412
现在，他们可能拥有相同的资源，也想实现相似的目标，但他们无法有效沟通，
这造成了协作和资源共享的障碍。
Now, they might have access to the same resources and they also want to accomplish similar goals,
but their inability to communicate effectively creates barriers to collaboration as well as resource sharing.

602
01:22:29,776 --> 01:22:40,228
现在，规划和行动模块对智能体的功能至关重要，因为它们涉及频繁的往返交互。
Now, the planning and action modules are absolutely essential to an agent's
functionality because they involve frequent back and forth interactions.

603
01:22:41,838 --> 01:22:51,428
现在，在典型的问题解决过程中，智能体可能会在规划和行动之间循环数十甚至上百次。
Now, during a typical problem solving session, an agent might cycle between planning and action dozens or even hundreds of times.

604
01:22:51,758 --> 01:22:56,420
规划模块分析当前情况，并决定下一步采取什么行动。
The planning modules analyze the current situation and decides what action to take next.

605
01:22:57,230 --> 01:23:01,188
行动模块执行该决策并反馈结果。
The action module executes that decision and reports back the results.

606
01:23:02,030 --> 01:23:07,460
规划模块随后将这些结果纳入其理解中，并决定下一步行动。
The planning module then incorporates those results into its understanding and decides on the next action.

607
01:23:08,206 --> 01:23:20,900
所以，这种规划与行动之间的持续对话，正是智能体能够根据现实世界的反馈来调整方法，
并有效处理复杂多步骤问题的核心。
So this continuous dialogue between planning and action is really what enables agents to adapt to their approach based on real-world
feedback and it can also handle complex multi-step problems effectively.

608
01:23:22,254 --> 01:23:30,176
然而，行动模块中的工具执行及其与规划的集成，往往是特定于实现的。
However, tool execution in the action module and its integration with planning are often implementation specific.

609
01:23:30,350 --> 01:23:43,268
现在，这意味着不同的智能体框架开发出了各自独特的定义工具、调用工具、
传递参数给工具以及解释工具结果的方法。
Now this means that different agent frameworks have developed their own unique ways of defining tools, calling tools,
passing parameters to tools, and also interpreting tool results.

610
01:23:44,558 --> 01:23:55,844
所以这些实现细节看起来可能只是细微的技术考量，但它们最终造成了巨大的互操作性障碍。
So these implementation details, they might seem like minor technical considerations,
but they do end up creating significant barriers to interoperability.

611
01:23:56,430 --> 01:24:05,124
所以当每个框架使用自己的惯例和协议时，为一种框架开发的工具就无法轻易被另一种框架使用。
So when each framework uses its own conventions and protocols, tools
developed for one framework cannot easily be used by another framework.

612
01:24:06,222 --> 01:24:11,204
现在，这最终导致了一个特别令人沮丧的情况。
Now, this does end up leading us to a particularly frustrating situation.

613
01:24:12,270 --> 01:24:26,788
虽然同样的工具在概念上可能适用于不同的智能体框架，但具体
的实现细节导致一个框架的规划-行动接口无法用于另一个框架。
Even though the same tools might be conceptually useful across different agent frameworks,
the implementation-specific details prevent the plan action interface from one framework being used with another framework.

614
01:24:27,502 --> 01:24:40,708
例如，为 LangGraph 开发的 Google Search 工具就不能直接插入到 CrewAI 智能体中，
尽管这两个智能体可能都受益于搜索互联网的能力。
So for example, a Google search tool that's developed for line graph cannot simply be plugged into a crew AI agent,
even though both agents might benefit from the ability to search the same internet.

615
01:24:41,966 --> 01:24:54,308
同样，为某个框架创建的数据库连接工具，若要与其他框架配合工作，
可能需要大量的修改甚至完全重新实现。
Similarly, a database connection tool created for one framework requires significant modification or maybe even a complete re
implementation to work with a different framework.

616
01:24:56,206 --> 01:25:04,900
这种缺乏互操作性的情况，给开发者以及构建 AI 智能体系统的组织带来了几个问题。
So, this lack of interoperability creates several problems for developers and also organizations building AI agent systems.

617
01:25:06,158 --> 01:25:14,180
首先，它会导致重复劳动，因为同样的工具必须为不同的框架多次重新实现。
First, it leads to duplicated effort as the same tools must be re-implemented multiple times for different frameworks.

618
01:25:15,630 --> 01:25:28,644
其次，它造成了供应商锁定，这意味着一旦选择了某个智能体框架，
你就完全被绑定在只能使用与其兼容或兼容的工具上。
Second, it creates vendor lock-in, where choosing one agent framework means that you're now completely committed to using only tools
that are capable or compatible with that framework.

619
01:25:29,390 --> 01:25:39,712
第三，它减缓了创新，因为开发者现在不得不花更多时间在技术集成上，
而不是专注于解决 Business 问题。
Third, it slows down innovation as developers are now trying to spend more time
on technical integration instead of just focusing on solving business problems.

620
01:25:39,982 --> 01:25:49,316
最后，它碎片化了 AI 智能体生态系统，阻碍了能够让整个社区受益的协作式工具开发。
Finally, it fragments the AI agent ecosystem, preventing the kind of
collaborative tool development that could really benefit the entire community.

621
01:25:50,510 --> 01:26:08,068
随着 AI 智能体变得越来越先进，且组织希望整合多个智能体框架或在不同框架之间切换而不损
失现有的工具投入，对具有互操作性的智能体工具的需求变得日益紧迫。
So the need for interoperable agent tooling has become increasingly urgent as AI agents become more sophisticated and also as
organizations want to integrate multiple agent frameworks or switch between frameworks without losing their existing tool investments.

622
01:26:09,422 --> 01:26:15,712
现在，这一挑战推动了智能体工具标准化方法的开发。
Now, this challenge has motivated the development of standardized approaches to agent tooling.

623
01:26:15,952 --> 01:26:19,300
那么，智能体 AI 的核心能力是什么？
Now, what are the key capabilities of agentic AI?

624
01:26:19,918 --> 01:26:21,232
它们是自主的。
They are autonomous.

625
01:26:21,518 --> 01:26:28,196
我所说的自主，是指它们基本上是在没有任何人工干预的情况下根据目标采取行动。
What I mean by autonomous is that they are basically acting on goals without any human input.

626
01:26:29,838 --> 01:26:32,612
一个例子可以是客服智能体。
An example could be a customer support agent.

627
01:26:33,390 --> 01:26:43,620
客服智能体，比如电信行业的客服智能体，负责回答客户的电话或邮件并解决他们的问题。
A customer support agent is let's say a telecom industry customer support
agent who answers calls or emails from customers and resolves their queries.

628
01:26:44,206 --> 01:26:49,060
为了做到这一点，它们的操作是提取来自某些内部系统的信息。
And to do that, what they do is pull info from, let's say, some internal systems.

629
01:26:49,262 --> 01:26:54,272
它们会查看客户资料、查看通话记录历史，以及类似的细节。
They will look at the customer profile, they look at their call log history, details like that.

630
01:26:54,510 --> 01:27:01,412
现在想象一下，这些操作被智能体 AI 自动化了，也就是我们正在讨论的自主智能体 AI。
Now imagine that being automated by agentic AI, which is the autonomous agentic AI that we are talking about.

631
01:27:02,126 --> 01:27:08,352
现在这个智能体 AI 可以查看查询请求，并自动从内部系统提取信息。
So now this agentic AI can look at the query and it can automatically pull info from internal systems.

632
01:27:08,558 --> 01:27:14,468
它可以更新工单，如果需要可以升级处理，还可以提醒人工人员并引入人机协同。
It can update tickets, it can escalate if needed, it can alert a human and bring the human in the loop.

633
01:27:14,926 --> 01:27:17,552
所以所有这些现在都是自主完成的。
So all that is now being done autonomously.

634
01:27:17,838 --> 01:27:26,756
它可以朝着特定目标行动，在这个案例中就是客户
体验和解决他们的查询，并且它可以一步步地完成。
So it can act on a certain goal, which is customer experience and
resolving their queries in this use case, and it can do it step by step.

635
01:27:27,502 --> 01:27:32,032
AI 智能体的另一个能力是多步规划。
And another capability of AI agents is multi-step planning.

636
01:27:32,206 --> 01:27:37,828
智能体 AI 可以做的就是将复杂的目标分解成子任务。
What agentic AI can do is it can break down complex goals into subtasks.

637
01:27:38,606 --> 01:27:41,872
所以，广义上来说，有三种类型的 AI。
So yes, there are broadly three types of AI.

638
01:27:42,062 --> 01:27:50,032
你可以用不同的方式对它们进行分类，但广义上你可以把它们分为三种不同类型的 AI。
You can classify them in different ways, but very broadly you can categorize them into three different types of AI.

639
01:27:50,272 --> 01:27:54,820
所以 AI 可以是，AI 可以是弱人工智能。
So AI can be well, AI can be narrow AI.

640
01:27:55,534 --> 01:27:58,340
这些是非常、非常特定于任务的。
So these are very, very task specific.

641
01:27:58,832 --> 01:28:00,832
这些是特定于任务的。
These are task specific.

642
01:28:01,262 --> 01:28:03,204
我说的特定于任务是什么意思？
What do I mean by task specific?

643
01:28:03,630 --> 01:28:09,072
所谓特定任务，我的意思是，假设你想在 YouTube 上搜索点什么。
By task specific, I mean let's say you are trying to search for something on YouTube.

644
01:28:09,312 --> 01:28:14,752
YouTube 能理解你的个人口味、你感兴趣的主题，然后它会进行筛选。
So YouTube understands your personal taste, your topics, and then it will curate.

645
01:28:14,912 --> 01:28:16,912
它会为你过滤搜索结果。
It will filter the search results for you.

646
01:28:17,102 --> 01:28:18,820
所以这就是非常特定的任务。
So it's very task specific.

647
01:28:19,438 --> 01:28:22,192
那么我们可以聊聊现在的聊天机器人。
So you can talk about the chatbots today.

648
01:28:22,382 --> 01:28:30,432
它所能做的只是理解你的一点历史记录，它能把文本切词，然后发送给 LLM 模型。
All it can do is understand a little bit of your history, and what it can do is tokenize the text and send it to the LLM model.

649
01:28:30,638 --> 01:28:35,748
所以 LLM 是完全不同类型的 AI，但我们现在不只是在谈论 Gen AI。
So LLM is a totally different type of AI, but we are not only talking about Gen AI.

650
01:28:36,032 --> 01:28:43,952
我们只是在谈论那些能对文本进行编码、嵌入和切词的聊天机器人。
We are only talking about chatbots where it can encode the text, it can embed the text, and it can tokenize it.

651
01:28:44,112 --> 01:28:51,792
所以这些都是这些 AI 应用能做的非常特定的任务，我们将其归类为弱人工智能。
So those are very task-specific things that these AI applications can do, which we categorize as narrow AI.

652
01:28:51,952 --> 01:28:56,132
然后还有 Gen AI，它可以创建新内容。
So then there is Gen AI, which can create new content.

653
01:28:56,558 --> 01:29:06,512
它可以生成文本、生成图像、生成代码，比如 ChatGPT 或 Dolly，还有 GitHub Copilot。
It can create text, it can create images, it can create code, it can create, for example, ChatGPT or Dolly, GitHub Copilot.

654
01:29:06,672 --> 01:29:08,352
这些全都是 Gen AI。
These are all Gen AI.

655
01:29:08,512 --> 01:29:13,540
所以对于 AI 有一种更具未来感的愿景，我们称之为通用人工智能。
So there is a more futuristic vision for AI, which we call general AI.

656
01:29:13,774 --> 01:29:14,672
那发生了什么呢？
So what happened?

657
01:29:14,832 --> 01:29:16,432
呃，我不是今天才出生的。
Uh I wasn't born today.

658
01:29:16,672 --> 01:29:19,152
AI 在我们的时代之前就已经存在了。
AI existed well before our time.

659
01:29:19,312 --> 01:29:22,592
甚至在二战期间，我们就有了 Alan Turing。
Even during World War II, we had Alan Turing.

660
01:29:23,022 --> 01:29:28,512
Alan Turing，基本上有一部关于他的非常精彩的电影。
Alan Turing is basically there is this beautiful movie about Alan Turing.

661
01:29:28,782 --> 01:29:30,244
我不记得片名了。
I can't remember the title.

662
01:29:30,926 --> 01:29:33,604
所以 Alan Turing 提出了 Turing test。
So Alan Turing coined the Turing test.

663
01:29:33,920 --> 01:29:35,600
对，甚至是在二战期间。
Right, even during World War II.

664
01:29:35,854 --> 01:29:37,188
那么 Turing test 是什么呢？
So what was the Turing test?

665
01:29:37,806 --> 01:29:42,400
Alan Turing 说，你有一个人类，然后你有一个计算机，对吧？
So Alan Turing said you have a human and then you have a computer, right?

666
01:29:42,574 --> 01:29:51,040
你有一个机器，你放上一个屏幕，人与计算机互动，并认为它实际上是人类，而不是计算机。
You have a machine and you put a screen up and the person interacts
with the computer and thinks it's actually a human, not a computer.

667
01:29:51,246 --> 01:29:58,160
所以如果满足这个条件，我们就说通过了 Turing test，这就是我们所说的 AI。
So if that condition is met, then we say the Turing test is passed, and this is what we call AI.

668
01:29:58,382 --> 01:30:00,708
所以 Alan Turing 提出了这个 Turing test。
So Alan Turing coined this Turing test.

669
01:30:02,510 --> 01:30:04,240
为了能够测试 AI。
To be able to test AI.

670
01:30:04,480 --> 01:30:11,300
真的，我们谈到当他们构思 AI 会是什么样时，他们实际上构思的是通用人工智能。
Really, we talked about how when they envisioned what AI would be, they were actually envisioning general AI.

671
01:30:11,694 --> 01:30:17,040
所以通用人工智能就是那种在各种任务中都能达到人类水平推理的 AI。
So general AI is where it's like human-level reasoning across tasks.

672
01:30:17,200 --> 01:30:19,652
它就像是超认知机器。
It's like hypercognitive machines.

673
01:30:20,000 --> 01:30:25,920
这就是大多数人的设想，这就是为什么它花了这么长时间才变成现实。
So that was what most people were envisioning, and that's why it took a long time to become a reality.

674
01:30:26,126 --> 01:30:28,080
首先，数据必须爆发式增长。
First of all, data had to explode.

675
01:30:28,302 --> 01:30:32,080
Cloud 计算必须变得更可行且更经济。
Cloud computing had to become more possible and more economical.

676
01:30:32,400 --> 01:30:35,760
所以这一切才有了今天世界的 AI。
So all of that led to the AI of today's world.

677
01:30:35,982 --> 01:30:39,268
这就是我对 AI 的大致分类。
So that's how I would broadly categorize what AI is.

678
01:30:39,534 --> 01:30:42,560
现在回到我们关于智能体 AI 的话题上。
So getting back to our topic on agent KI.

679
01:30:43,278 --> 01:30:48,080
所以，各位，正如我所说，智能体 AI 是自主的，它可以制定多步骤计划。
So Agent AKI, folks, like I said, is autonomous and it can do multi-step plan.

680
01:30:49,070 --> 01:30:57,252
它可以将复杂的目标分解为可执行的子任务，并且可以与任何环境交互。
It can break down complex goals into executable subtasks, and it can interact with any environment.

681
01:30:57,870 --> 01:31:05,360
我的意思是，它可以使用 Tool，可以使用第三方应用程序，也可以通过 APIs 来执行行动。
What I mean by that is it can use tools, it can use third-party applications, it can use APIs to act.

682
01:31:05,600 --> 01:31:12,960
比如，让我的智能体，也就是我的 AI 智能体，为一名八年级的学生写一个科学项目的创意。
